#---
# purpose: "a map pattern selects a clause on every door, in function heads and in case"
# oracle: oracle.exs
#---
#
# # map_clause_dispatch
#
# Map patterns reach dispatch through two region kinds — `map_kind`, which asks
# whether the subject is a map at all, and `map_key`, which asks whether a
# particular key is present — and both are decided separately by each of the
# three doors.
#
# Until this fixture, every behavioural fixture exercising either of them
# matched a map inside a `receive`, so both regions were covered only on the
# receive matcher and never on entry dispatch. That is the same blind spot that
# let entry dispatch ship a `Region::Bitstring` arm which merely returned
# "does not support bitstring tests yet": the variant was handled, the handling
# was a stub, and no fixture ran it. Exhaustive matching forces an arm to
# exist; only a fixture forces it to be right.
#
# Entry-dispatch map matching is correct today. This fixture is here so it
# cannot stop being correct quietly.
#
# ## What it covers
#
#   * clause selection on the presence of a key, and on a key's value;
#   * a bare `%{}` pattern, which matches any map because a map pattern is a
#     subset test rather than an exact shape;
#   * clause order mattering — a more specific pattern ahead of `%{}`;
#   * a non-map argument falling through to a wildcard, which is the `map_kind`
#     question rather than the `map_key` one;
#   * the same shapes in `case`, which reaches the same dispatch;
#   * a map with non-atom keys, and one with more keys than the pattern names.
def main() do
  dbg(kind(%{tag: :a, value: 7}))
  dbg(kind(%{tag: :b}))
  dbg(kind(%{tag: :b, extra: 1}))
  dbg(kind(%{other: 1}))
  dbg(kind(%{}))
  dbg(kind(42))
  dbg(kind([1, 2]))

  dbg(lookup(%{"name" => "ada", "age" => 36}))
  dbg(lookup(%{"age" => 36}))

  dbg(described(%{tag: :a, value: 9}))
  dbg(described(%{value: 9}))
  dbg(described(:not_a_map))
end

defp kind(%{tag: :a, value: v}), do: {:a, v}
defp kind(%{tag: :b}), do: :b
defp kind(%{}), do: :some_map
defp kind(_other), do: :not_a_map

defp lookup(%{"name" => name}), do: {:named, name}
defp lookup(%{}), do: :anonymous

defp described(subject) do
  case subject do
    %{tag: :a, value: v} -> {:case_a, v}
    %{value: v} -> {:case_value, v}
    %{} -> :case_map
    _other -> :case_other
  end
end
